    "title": "How to Build a Healthy Credit Score",
    "imageURL": "https://i.ibb.co/DgQQTR48/img01.jpg",
    "shortDescription": "Easy habits that help you build and maintain a strong credit profile.",
    "body": "A healthy credit score is not built overnight—it is the result of consistent financial habits. The most important factors include paying bills on time, keeping credit utilization low (below 30%), avoiding unnecessary hard inquiries, and maintaining older accounts to grow your credit age.\n\nYou should also monitor your credit report regularly. Many people discover errors—incorrect balances, unknown accounts, or outdated late payments.\n\n**Quick tips:**\n• Pay your bills before the due date.\n• Keep your credit card usage under 30%.\n• Do not open too many new accounts at once.\n• Check your credit report at least twice per year.\n\nImproving your credit score helps reduce loan interest rates and increases your financial stability."
